In SAP CPI, the MIME Multipart Encoder transforms a message into a multipart format, while the
MIME Multipart Decoder converts a multipart message back into a standard message with attachments.
The encoder prepares a message for transmission that may include attachments, while the decoder
reconstructs the original message from the multipart parts.

MIME Multipart Encoder:
Purpose: Takes a message, potentially with attachments, and converts it into a MIME multipart format.
How it works: Packages the message body as the first part and any attachments as subsequent parts of the multipart message.
Output: A MIME multipart message with a Content-Type header indicating multipart.


MIME Multipart Decoder:
Purpose: Takes a MIME multipart message and transforms it back into a standard message with attachments.
How it works: Extracts the first part of the multipart message as the main message body and any remaining parts as attachments.
Output: A standard message with the extracted body and attachments.